      "source_url": "https://thaqalayn.net/hadith/34/4/18/14",
      "text": [
        "4839 - وَ فِي رِوَايَةِ اَلسَّكُونِيِّ قَالَ قَالَ عَلِيٌّ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ : فِي رَجُلٍ آلَى مِنِ اِمْرَأَتِهِ وَ ظَاهَرَ فِي كَلِمَةٍ وَاحِدَةٍ قَالَ \"عَلَيْهِ كَفَّارَةٌ وَاحِدَةٌ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.4839 - In the narration of Al-Sakuni, he said that Imam Ali ibn Abi Talib (as) was asked about a man who both swore an oath (ilaʾ) and declared ẓihar (a form of divorce by comparison) against his wife in a single statement.\nImam (as) said: \"He is obligated to offer only one expiation.\""
        ]
      }
    },
